Description: Read Redis username from values instead of a secret key
 The template sourced AP_REDIS_USER from a 'username' key in the Redis secret,
 but neither the chart's own secrets.yaml nor the Bitnami redis subchart ever
 creates that key — so the container failed to start with CreateContainerConfigError
 whenever activepieces.redis.username was set. The username is not sensitive
 (the password is, and is still read from the secret), so take it from values.
Author: Gentian Platform <platform@gentian.org>
Origin: other, https://github.com/gentian-org/gentian-apps
Forwarded: not-yet
Bug-Upstream: none filed
Applied-Upstream: no
Last-Update: 2026-08-06
---
diff --git a/templates/_podSpec.tpl b/templates/_podSpec.tpl
index 71e34c1..bda92e6 100644
--- a/templates/_podSpec.tpl
+++ b/templates/_podSpec.tpl
@@ -79,10 +79,7 @@ template:
           {{- if and (eq .Values.activepieces.queue.mode "redis") (or .Values.activepieces.redis.password .Values.activepieces.redis.existingSecret) }}
           {{- if .Values.activepieces.redis.username }}
           - name: AP_REDIS_USER
-            valueFrom:
-              secretKeyRef:
-                name: {{ default (include "activepieces.secrets.redis" .) .Values.activepieces.redis.existingSecret }}
-                key: username
+            value: {{ .Values.activepieces.redis.username | quote }}
           {{- end }}
           - name: AP_REDIS_PASSWORD
             valueFrom:
